@lens(user, developer)
| The small executable layer: what code in `do` blocks does, processes and files, tasks run by path, and funcs, macros and templates. It's kept small on purpose: code decides, combines and calls, real work runs in the language a system is built in, and what stays is deterministic, so every run is replayable.
